  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.2 stable: rollup of rc.1 + rc.2 + rc.3 + the SCTP backpressure polling fix shipped in commit `7fd70c5`. Five SCTP / wire correctness improvements over 3.2.1, no breaking changes. (1) **SCTP backpressure shared-TCS multi-awaiter fix.** `_bufferedAmountLowTcs` is now a shared TCS that every concurrent `Send` references at await time. `OnBufferedAmountLow` completes the shared TCS to release ALL awaiters, then atomically installs a fresh TCS for the next round. Replaces the rc.1 `Interlocked.Exchange`-per-awaiter pattern that orphaned all but the latest concurrent awaiter and timed out at 30s in P2P's 8-chunk pipeline pattern. (2) **`RtcPeer.Send` polling-based wait.** `OnBufferedAmountLow` is best-effort - `DesktopRTCDataChannel`'s 20ms poller only fires on strict above-then-below transitions; rapid SCTP drains miss the transition entirely. `Send` now races the event TCS against a 50ms `Task.Delay` so the next iteration's top-of-loop `BufferedAmount` re-check breaks out when drained. The 120-second wall-clock ceiling covers genuinely-stalled SCTP rather than relying on an event we can't trust. Closes `LargeBuffer_100MB_DispatchedOverRealWebRtc_BitExact` (was failing reliably at 1m37s-7m7s with `TimeoutException` despite `BufferedAmount=0` and `ReadyState=open`; now PASSES in ~5 min). (3) **Duplicate-handshake hardening on Wire.OnHandshake.** Phantom destroyed-wire entries no longer linger in `_wiresByBtPeerId[canonical]`; bridge `RemoveWhere(w => w.Destroyed)` filter on close. Closes `P2PSwarm.TwoTab_PeerDiscovery`'s peerCount-stuck-at-1 regression. (4) **SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.8 stable dep bump** - pulls in Desktop OnBufferedAmountLow now actually firing + browser connection-state polling fallback + opt-in DiagnosticsEnabled. (5) Diagnostic groundwork: `[RtcPeer][BACKPRESSURE-DIAG]` instrumentation. Verified via SpawnDev.ILGPU.P2P real-WebRTC integration tests.",
